INT. CABLE-CAR SUMMIT STATION - CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

Wind hums in the cables. Frost on the glass. A space heater ticks.

INGRID VOSS, 50s, station operator, grey braid, both hands around a steel thermos. She watches a bank of monitors.

KOFI OSEI, 20s, apprentice mechanic, grease on his cuffs, sits on a crate eating crackers.

Quiet. Too quiet.

KOFI
Last car's late.

INGRID
Snow on the line.

KOFI
You said that an hour ago.

INGRID
It was snowing an hour ago.

He laughs. She doesn't.

On the monitor: a single gondola, CAR 7, crawling up through the dark.

KOFI (CONT'D)
One passenger?

INGRID
One ticket. Cash.

Kofi crunches a cracker. Brushes crumbs off his knee.

KOFI
Who rides up at midnight?

INGRID
Someone who wants the view.

The radio on the desk CRACKLES.

HALVORSEN (V.O.)
(over radio, thin)
Base to summit. Ingrid, you there?

Ingrid thumbs the key.

INGRID
Go ahead, Halvorsen.

HALVORSEN (V.O.)
Quick check. You got Car 7 on your board?

INGRID
Coming up now.

Silence on the line. Static. Too long.

HALVORSEN (V.O.)
Ingrid. Car 7 is in the depot.

Kofi stops chewing.

INGRID
Say again.

HALVORSEN (V.O.)
Seven's parked. Locked out since six. I'm looking at it.

Ingrid's eyes go to the monitor. The car climbs. Closer.

KOFI
Then what is that?

INGRID
Kill the lights.

KOFI
What?

INGRID
Kill them.

He slaps the wall switch. Dark. Only the monitors glow.

Bolt of cold air. The stairwell door at the back, open an inch. It was shut.

Kofi sees it. Freezes.

KOFI
(whispering)
Somebody's already up here.

A gloved hand pushes the door wide.

BASHIR NAZARI, 30s, ski jacket, no skis, steps in. Calm hands. Wet boots. A ticket stub between two fingers.

BASHIR
Evening.

INGRID
You came up the service stairs.

BASHIR
Eleven hundred steps. I like the exercise.

KOFI
Then who's in the car?

BASHIR
Ah.

He checks his watch.

BASHIR (CONT'D)
That'll be Lenka.

The glass behind them shudders. Car 7 slams into the dock. Doors hiss open.

LENKA DROZD, 40s, shaved head, black coveralls, a coil of cable ties over one shoulder, steps out of the empty-looking cabin. Unhurried.

LENKA
Sorry. Traffic.

Ingrid backs against the desk. Her hand finds the radio.

INGRID
(low, to the radio)
Halvorsen. Don't send anyone.

HALVORSEN (V.O.)
(tight)
Already sent. Two minutes.

LENKA
No. It's four. Your cable's cold.

She smiles at Kofi.

LENKA (CONT'D)
Crackers. Good. Long night.

Bashir locks the stairwell door. Click.

Ingrid lifts the thermos. Sets it down. Slowly.

INGRID
What do you want?

BASHIR
The ledger.

INGRID
There is no ledger.

BASHIR
Ingrid. Your husband said you'd say that.

Her face doesn't move. Kofi looks at her.

KOFI
Husband?

Wind drops. The heater ticks. The cable above them goes still.
